```

---

## 🚀 How to Run

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/somendrew/Fraud-Transaction-Detection.git
cd Fraud-Transaction-Detection

# Install dependencies
pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn matplotlib seaborn imbalanced-learn

# Open the notebook
jupyter notebook FraudTransactionDetection3.ipynb
```

**Dataset:** Available [here](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-zOKe7FjKdpahCgpRKhDQwvVPNNkVKQB/view?usp=sharing)

---

## 💡 Key Learnings

- Working with severely imbalanced datasets requires special evaluation metrics beyond accuracy
- Ensemble methods (Random Forest, XGBoost) significantly outperform linear models on tabular fraud data
- Feature scaling is critical for distance-based and linear models

